 the OR logic handles it properly. The CONCAT approach with null handling actually works reliably across dialects, but I'll stick with the `<choose>` approach since it's more explicit and safer. I need to apply the same pattern to `countBySearch` as well, then set up the mapper interface with `@Param` annotations for multi-parameter methods.\n\nDefining the mapper interface methods...\n\nNow I'm thinking about the column name mapping issue—the database uses snake_case like `hire_date` and `created_at`, but the Java entity uses camelCase. MyBatis won't auto-map these by default unless I enable `mapUnderscoreToCamelCase`, which isn't currently set in the config. Rather than adding column aliases throughout the SQL, I'll create a resultMap in the XML file to handle the mapping explicitly.\n\nI also notice the directory structure has a discrepancy—the spec shows `mapper/` (singular) but the implementation plan and DatabaseConfig both use `mappers/` (plural), so I'll go with the plural form to match the existing configuration.\n\nFor the `updated_at` field, I'll let the database handle it on insert since the schema defaults to CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, but I'll explicitly set it during updates.\n\nWriting the mapper XML now... Writing the mapper XML... Writing the mapper methods... Writing the search queries...\n\nNow I'm realizing I need to handle the test infrastructure setup first since the mapper tests depend on it. The CLAUDE.md guidelines emphasize writing tests alongside implementation, so I should prioritize getting the TestAppConfig in place before tackling the integration tests for the mapper. I need to focus on Item 6 alone for this session—implementing the mapper interface and XML file, then verifying everything compiles and existing tests still pass with `mvn compile` and `mvn test`.\n\nNow I'll update the implementation plan to mark Item 6 as in progress.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_toke